# Xmen Copilot Architecture & Development Guide

## Project Overview

Xmen Copilot is an AI-powered assistant built with Next.js, React, TypeScript, and modern UI/UX frameworks. It provides chat-based interactions, context management, and integrating Mistral AI and OpenAI to enhance X-MEN (application instance management business system) with copilot functionality and function calling capabilities.



### Core Architecture
The core follows a clear hierarchical structure:

1. **Webview** (components/copilot/*): Manages the webview lifecycle and communication
2. **Controller** (core/controller/index.js): Handles webview messages and task management
3. **Task** (core/task/index.js): Executes API requests and tool operations

This architecture provides clear separation of concerns:
- Webview focuses on webview UI/UX integration
- Controller manages state and coordinates tasks
- Task handles the execution of AI requests and tool operations

## Task Execution System

